                                "sense_id": "3fe5b21f-696d-32c9-9edd-6ffc49482d4c",
                                "text": "In plants, the ability to recognize self from nonself plays an important role in fertilization, […]. Many genes with reproductive roles also have antibacterial and immune functions, which indicate that the threat of microbial attack on the sperm or egg may be a major influence on rapid evolution during reproduction."
